                <pb facs="0223" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">842.612 Peaches/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Ottawa</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-08T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your despatch No. 22, July 18, 1927, stated Motherwell promised decision
                    respecting peach embargo by July 21. Please telegraph status of this matter.
                    Peach interests are pressing for action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
